Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:08:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): a ball nose's corner radius is its ball - shown,
 not edited

A ball nose's tip is a sphere, so its corner radius is half the
diameter, and every reader already used that number whatever the field
held (Cutter::of, Tool::profile, the stock sim's sphere atom). The tool
editor still offered an editable "Corner radius" that changed nothing,
and a draft retyped from an end mill saved a ball with corner 0.

- Tool::tip_corner_r states the law: a ball's (or probe's) corner is
  d/2, every other kind answers its own field.
- The editor shows the ball's corner as text with no field to edit.
- ToolUi::to_tool saves a ball with corner_r = d/2, so the document
  says what is cut; ToolUi::tool_kind names the draft's kind.
- The library summary reads tip_corner_r.

Fixes #263

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
